[{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x-1)\\ln(2x+y),\\qquad y(1)=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use the Euler formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_r+h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to obtain an approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Using your answer to part a), use the formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to obtain <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer to three decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,y_0=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =2+0.5\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =2+0.5\\times0=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =1+0.5=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(2) =2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =2+2\\times0.5\\times0.8047189562\\ldots=2.804718956\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =1.5+0.5=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(2) =2.805\\ (3\\text{ DP})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x+\\ln(1+y),\\qquad y(2)=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Use Euler's step by step method once, followed by using the midpoint formula</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r),\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to obtain an approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2.2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer to three decimal places.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =2,y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+0.1\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+0.1\\times2.693147181\\ldots=1.269314718\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =2+0.1=2.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+2\\times0.1\\times2.9194779\\ldots=1.58389558\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =2.1+0.1=2.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(2.2) =1.584\\ (3\\text{ DP})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Given a second point has already been found using Euler's step by step method, use the midpoint formula</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r),\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following, giving your answers to three decimal places:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y\\times2^x,(0,1),(0.75,1.75)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.75\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y\\tan x,(1,0.2),(1.25,0.2779)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1.75)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0.75,y_1=1.75\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+2\\times0.75\\times2.943137453\\ldots=5.41470618\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(1.5) =5.415\\ (3\\text{ DP})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,y_0=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =1.25,y_1=0.2779\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.2+2\\times0.25\\times0.8363594124\\ldots=0.6181797062\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =1.25+0.25=1.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_3 =y_1+2h\\mathrm f(x_2,y_2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.2779+2\\times0.25\\times8.71721164\\ldots=4.63650582\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(1.75) =4.637\\ (3\\text{ DP})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Use the improved Euler's formula</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_r+\\frac12(k_1+k_2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_1=h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r),k_2=h\\mathrm f(x_r+h,y_r+k_1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following. In each case the curve satisfies the given differential equation and passes through the given point. Give your answer to three significant figures:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\ln(2x+\\sqrt{y}),(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x-\\cos^2y,(2,0.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(2.2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(3x+2)\\sqrt{x+y},y(0)=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q5: Separation of Variables</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,y_0=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =2.633916794\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =4.2501647216535\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =3,\\quad y_1=3+\\frac12(2.633916794\\ldots+4.2501647216535\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\phantom{=3,\\quad y_1}=6.442040258\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(3) =6.44\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =2,y_0=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =0.2459397694\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =0.3321224914\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =2.2,\\quad y_1=0.5+\\frac12(0.2459397694\\ldots+0.3321224914\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\phantom{=2.2,\\quad y_1}=0.7890461304\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(2.2) =0.789\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,y_0=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =1.732050808\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =4.002893403\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =3,\\quad y_1=3+\\frac12(1.732050808\\ldots+4.002893403\\ldots)=5.867472105\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(0.5) =5.87\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A curve passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,e^{0.1})\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and satisfies the differential equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y\\sqrt{2x+1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use Euler's step by step method once, then the midpoint formula</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r),\\quad x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>once, each with a step length of 0.1 to estimate the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Give your answer to three decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Find the particular solution of the differential equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y\\sqrt{2x+1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln y=\\mathrm g(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is function to be found.</p></li><li><p>Find the relative error of your approximation in part a) giving your answer to two significant figures.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q6: First Order Linear Differential Equations</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =4,y_0=e^{0.1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =e^{0.1}+0.1\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =e^{0.1}+0.1\\times3.315512754\\ldots=1.436722193\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =4+0.1=4.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =e^{0.1}+2\\times0.1\\times4.357794176\\ldots=1.97672953\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =4.1+0.1=4.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(4.2) =1.977\\ (3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\frac1y\\,dy=\\int\\sqrt{2x+1}\\,dx=\\int(2x+1)^{1/2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\ln y=\\frac13(2x+1)^{3/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,e^{0.1})\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\ln(e^{0.1})=\\frac13(2\\times4+1)^{3/2}+c\\Rightarrow c=-8.9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\ln y=\\frac13(2x+1)^{3/2}-8.9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1.977-e^{\\frac13(2\\times4.2+1)^{3/2}-8.9}}{e^{\\frac13(2\\times4.2+1)^{3/2}-8.9}}=-0.025\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>A curve passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and satisfies the differential equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x-\\frac12y\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use Euler's step by step method once, then the midpoint formula</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r),\\quad x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>once, each with a step length of 0.05 to estimate the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the general solution of the differential equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x-\\frac12y\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies the differential equation in part b) and that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on the curve, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Comment on your accuracy in part a)</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+0.05\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+0.05\\times-\\frac12=0.975\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+0.05=0.05\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+2\\times0.05\\times-0.4375=0.95625\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =0.05+0.05=0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(0.1) =0.95625\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac12y=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>I.F. is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^{\\int\\frac12\\,dx}=e^{x/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"e^{x/2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac12e^{x/2}y=xe^{x/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"e^{x/2}y=\\int xe^{x/2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use Integration by Parts:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u=x,\\quad\\frac{dv}{dx}=e^{x/2},\\quad\\frac{du}{dx}=1,\\quad v=2e^{x/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\int xe^{x/2}\\,dx=2xe^{x/2}-\\int2e^{x/2}\\,dx=2xe^{x/2}-4e^{x/2}(+c)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So that:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"e^{x/2}y=2xe^{x/2}-4e^{x/2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2x-4+ce^{-x/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1=0-4+c\\Rightarrow c=5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y=2x-4+5e^{-x/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0.1,y=2\\times0.1-4+5e^{-0.1/2}=0.956147\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(0.1)=0.956\\ (3\\text{ SF})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The value from part a) is equal to the answer in part c) to three significant figures, meaning the estimate in part a) is very accurate.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A patient's drug concentration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mg/L in the bloodstream changes over time (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours) according to both metabolism and a slow continuous infusion. The rate of change of concentration satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dt}+0.2C=1.5e^{-0.1t}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Initially, the patient's drug concentration is 0 mg/L</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use Euler's method, with a step size of 0.5, to find an approximation for the drug concentration after 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p>Explain how the numerical method used in part a) could be made more accurate.</p></li><li><p>Refine the approximation found in part a) using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_r+\\frac12(k_1+k_2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_1=h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_2=h\\mathrm f(x_r+h,y_r+k_1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with a step size of 0.5. Give your answer to two significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dC}{dt} =-0.2C+1.5e^{-0.1t}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =0,C_0=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C_1 =0+0.5\\mathrm f(t_0,C_0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0+0.5\\times1.5=0.75\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore C =0.75\\text{ mg/L}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>A greater number of smaller steps could be used.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =0,C_0=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)=0.5\\mathrm f(t_0,C_0)=0.5\\times1.5=0.75\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =h\\mathrm f(x_r+h,y_r+k_1)=0.5\\mathrm f(0.5,0.75)=0.6384220684\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{r+1} =y_r+\\frac12(k_1+k_2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C_1 =0+\\frac12(0.75+0.6384220684\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.6942110342\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =0+0.5=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore C =0.69\\text{ mg/L}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The temperature <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span>(<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>C) of a chemical solution at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> minutes is modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(15-0.04t^2)\\frac{dT}{dt}+0.8T=6t\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The initial temperature of the solution is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>C.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use Euler's method, with a step size of 0.5, to find an approximation for the temperature of the solution after 1 minute, giving your answer to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Explain how the numerical method used in part a) could be made more accurate.</p></li><li><p>Refine the approximation found in part a) using the formula</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{n+1}=y_n+h\\mathrm f\\left(x_n+\\frac h2,y_n+\\frac h2\\mathrm f(x_n,y_n)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>with a step size of 1. Give your answer to three significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(15-0.04t^2)\\frac{dT}{dt}=6t-0.8T\\Rightarrow\\frac{dT}{dt}=\\frac{6t-0.8T}{15-0.04t^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =0,T_0=20\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_1 =20+0.5\\mathrm f(t_0,T_0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =20+0.5\\times-\\frac{16}{15}=19.46666667\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_1 =0+0.5=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_2 =19.46666667\\ldots+0.5\\mathrm f(t_1,T_1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =19.46666667\\ldots+0.5\\times-0.8387814098\\ldots=19.04727596\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_2 =0.5+0.5=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore T =19.0^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>A greater number of smaller steps could be used.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0 =0,T_0=20\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t_0+\\frac h2 =0+\\frac12=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"T_0+\\frac h2\\mathrm f(t_0,T_0) =20+\\frac12\\times-\\frac{16}{15}=19.46666667\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore T_1 =T_0+h\\mathrm f\\left(t_0+\\frac h2,T_0+\\frac h2\\mathrm f(t_0,T_0)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =20+1\\times\\mathrm f(0.5,19.46666667\\ldots)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =20+1\\times-0.8382222222\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =19.161777777\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore T =19.2^\\circ\\mathrm C\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x-y\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>with the initial condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The fourth-order Runge-Kutta method is defined by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_{n+1}=y_n+\\frac h6(k_1+2k_2+2k_3+k_4)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_1=\\mathrm f(x_n,y_n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2=\\mathrm f\\left(x_n+\\frac h2,y_n+\\frac h2k_1\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_3=\\mathrm f\\left(x_n+\\frac h2,y_n+\\frac h2k_2\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_4=\\mathrm f(x_n+h,y_n+hk_3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Use the fourth-order Runge-Kutta method with step length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to obtain an approximation to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(0.5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Give your answer to three decimal places.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)=\\mathrm f(0,1)=0-1=-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =\\mathrm f(x_0+0.25,y_0+0.25\\times-1)=\\mathrm f(0.25,0.75)=0.25-0.75=-0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_3 =\\mathrm f(x_0+0.25,y_0+0.25\\times-0.5)=\\mathrm f(0.25,0.875)=-0.625\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_4 =\\mathrm f(x_0+0.5,y_0+0.5\\times-0.625)=\\mathrm f(0.5,0.6875)=-0.1875\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+\\frac1{12}(-1+2(-0.5)+2(-0.625)-0.1875)=0.713541666\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y =0.714\\ (3\\text{ DP})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A curve passing through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,a)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=5x-y\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Applying Euler's step by step method once using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, followed by the formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> once from starting point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,a)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives an estimate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3.05\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h =0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,y_0=a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =a+0.1\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)=a+0.1\\times(5-a)=0.9a+0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =1+0.1=1.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)=a+0.2\\times(5.5-(0.9a+0.5))=0.82a+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow0.82a+1 =3.05\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a =2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x^2-y\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>and the condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y(1)=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. After applying Euler's step by step method once, it is found that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_1=0.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer to one decimal place.</p></li><li><p>Use the improved Euler's method, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x_2,y_2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =1,y_0=0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =0.5+h\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)=0.5+h\\times(1-0.5)=0.5h+0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_1=0.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5h+0.5=0.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore h=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =1+0.2=1.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =y_0+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)=0.5+2\\times0.2(1.2^2-0.6)=0.836\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_2 =1.2+0.2=1.4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore(x_1,y_1) =(1.4,0.836)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A curve passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x+y\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Applying Euler's step by step method once, followed by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_{r-1}+2h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_{r+1}=x_r+h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> once it is found that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_2=1.96\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+h\\mathrm f(x_0,y_0)=1+h\\times(0+1)=1+h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_1 =0+h=h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_2 =1+2h\\mathrm f(x_1,y_1)=1+2h\\times(1+h+h)=4h^2+2h+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_2=1.96\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4h^2+2h+1=1.96\\Rightarrow4h^2+2h-0.96=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow h=-0.8\\text{ or }h=0.3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore h=0.3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A curve which passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,a)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant, satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2y-3x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_r+\\frac12(k_1+k_2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_1=h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_2=h\\mathrm f(x_r+h,y_r+k_1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with starting point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,a)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives an estimate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=7.625\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h =0.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =2,y_0=a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =0.5(2a-6)=a-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =0.5(2(a+a-3)-3(2+0.5))=2a-6.75\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =a+\\frac12(a-3+2a-6.75)=2.5a-4.875\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore y(2.5) =7.625\\Rightarrow2.5a-4.875=7.625\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore a =5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.66-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>A curve passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and satisfies</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4y+2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The formula <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_{r+1}=y_r+\\frac12(k_1+k_2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_1=h\\mathrm f(x_r,y_r)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k_2=h\\mathrm f(x_r+h,y_r+k_1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is used to find that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y_1=2.16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> exactly. Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_0 =0,y_0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_1 =h(4+0)=4h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k_2 =h(4(1+4h)+2h)=18h^2+4h\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y_1 =1+\\frac12(4h+18h^2+4h)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore1+\\frac12(4h+18h^2+4h) =2.16\\Rightarrow9h^2+4h-1.16=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow h =-0.6444444\\ldots\\text{ or }h=0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore h =0.2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]